WEBVTT

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:14.990
Who are you working with?!

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:17.780
Your homeland sold you out.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.750
There's no longer any need 
to keep your allegiance.

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:26.460
Make this easy on yourself.
Tell us everything you know.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:29.180
You damned...

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:30.920
Monster!

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:41.060
Is he really a spy?

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:43.150
Without a doubt.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:27.030
Where... Where is he?!

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:41.410
<i>As the embers of world war smoldered</i>

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:43.910
<i>in autumn of 1937,</i>

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:46.000
<i>the Imperial Army</i>

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:46.620
<b>Greater East Asia 
Cultural Society</b>

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.080
<i>established a clandestine 
spy training agency.</i>

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:49.330
<b>Greater East Asia 
Cultural Society</b>

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:52.360
<i>The histories, names, and even ages</i>

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:56.010
<i>of the elite men who pass its 
rigorous application process</i>

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:59.450
<i>are all treated as top-secret information.</i>

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:03.680
<i>They easily complete training 
exercises that push them</i>

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.890
<i>to their physical and mental limits.</i>

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:09.060
<i>Under the command of founder 
Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki,</i>

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:11.900
<i>they operate worldwide, within the shadows.</i>

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:16.440
<i>And so a brand-new intelligence 
agency was created.</i>

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.090
<i>Its name is "D-Agency."</i>

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:59.760
Episode 11 - Coffin

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:17.420
I'm here.

00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:22.370
Colonel Wolff.

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:24.570
Your report,

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.510
Lieutenant Bauer.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:32.540
This program is a work of fiction. 
The characters, organizations, locations, laws, names, 
etc. being portrayed are unrelated to actual events.

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:29.230
It's been determined that the train crashed

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:32.000
because a signal light failed 
due to faulty power lines.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:34.880
There is no chance it was terrorism.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:37.940
These men were likely nothing 
more than onlookers.

00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:42.260
Inspect number three again. Thoroughly.

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:45.050
But there's no chance...

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:49.430
Pay particular attention to 
the matches he was carrying.

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:59.240
We found quinine on the 
matchbook in your wallet.

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:03.740
If you wrote a message with these 
and applied the right chemicals,

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:06.450
the words would become visible.

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:08.540
I-I know nothing of that...

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:09.800
Those matches...

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:12.010
I just picked them up.

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:13.000
Where?!

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.690
N-Near the site of the crash.

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:18.070
Despite the fact you don't smoke?

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:23.190
We didn't see a pipe or 
cigarettes in your belongings.

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:27.310
No tobacco resin under 
your fingernails, either.

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:31.620
This is too nice a wallet to be yours.

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:33.680
Who did you steal it from?

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:38.300
I swear it wasn't from one of our own.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.100
It was an Asian man!

00:05:40.510 --> 00:05:43.630
And besides, he was already dead.

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:45.490
What was his name?

00:05:45.770 --> 00:05:49.060
He must've had a card in his wallet.

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:52.340
I threw it away...

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:55.030
I believe it started

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:57.220
with an "M."

00:05:57.550 --> 00:06:01.020
Uh... Ma, Maku...

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:02.660
Maki...

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:04.190
Yes, that's it!

00:06:04.190 --> 00:06:05.460
That was the name!

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:12.690
Katsuhiko Maki. Japanese.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:14.810
This must be him.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:18.520
<b>Dead</b>

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:20.180
Let's go.

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:23.770
Colonel.

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:26.320
What should we do with him?

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:30.820
If nothing else, the blood of our 
countrymen has been spilled,

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:35.360
and our great and glorious nation 
cannot be held responsible.

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:37.160
We need a scapegoat.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:40.270
Turn him over to the Gestapo.

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:49.100
Search Maki's house,

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:52.290
but don't let the locals see 
what it is you're up to.

00:06:52.590 --> 00:06:54.660
Cordon off the surrounding area

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:57.050
and arrest anyone who seems suspicious.

00:06:57.050 --> 00:07:00.140
I'm going to need a lot of men for all that.

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:01.280
That's fine.

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:08.280
Investigate Katsuhiko Maki's work history,

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:11.250
and confirm that he's truly 
dead with your own eyes.

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:11.950
Sir.

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:34.700
Anything?

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:39.700
Nothing we've found suggests he was a spy.

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:42.470
Continuing to search would 
likely be a waste of time.

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:46.820
Colonel Wolff has caught over 
a hundred spies in his career.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:48.680
But this time...

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:50.230
Keep looking!

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:00.030
Colonel.

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:02.560
Sorry for the delay.

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:10.010
Maki Katsuhiko, 28,

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:12.150
single, no roommates.

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:14.080
He was an art dealer.

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:15.830
He registered about a year ago.

00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:18.510
He's from an affluent Japanese family

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:20.930
and came to Europe to study art.

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:24.100
After school, his interest in the field grew,

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:26.580
and he started his own art business.

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:29.580
The cause of death was shock

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:31.780
and blood loss after being pierced by

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:33.780
a steel beam broken off the train.

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:38.240
He probably looks so calm 
because he died instantly.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:42.270
And you're certain that's Maki?

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:45.090
I showed the picture to his 
neighbors and had them confirm.

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:47.480
They say it's definitely Maki.

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:48.800
Still...

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:50.310
What?

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:54.760
I was surprised to see that he 
was such a handsome fellow.

00:08:55.170 --> 00:08:59.200
And one person said, 
"He looks more alive in death."

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:04.440
Friends and relatives of the accident victims

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:06.150
have been visiting the hospital,

00:09:06.510 --> 00:09:08.780
but no one's come to see Maki.

00:09:11.540 --> 00:09:13.190
If I may, sir.

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:17.290
We examined all his belongings,

00:09:17.770 --> 00:09:20.660
but couldn't find anything suspicious at all.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:23.680
Perhaps it's more likely this Maki

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:27.060
really was just a simple 
art dealer, after all?

00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:31.580
Katsuhiko Maki is a Japanese spy.

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:33.170
There's no room for doubt.

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:34.180
But...

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:45.810
It's aspirin.

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:48.820
We found some in his belongings, as well.

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:52.090
He probably left them on 
the floor on purpose.

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:55.520
A trap to check if anyone had been

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:57.850
inside his house while he was away.

00:10:03.610 --> 00:10:06.770
Another trap of the same nature.

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:11.250
But I've heard that behind the scenes,

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:14.920
we've formed a three-way 
alliance with Japan and Italy.

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:17.690
Why on earth would a spy from Japan,

00:10:17.690 --> 00:10:21.430
a nation friendly to us, 
be sneaking into our country?

00:10:22.020 --> 00:10:24.160
Japan? Friendly?

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:28.670
Twenty-two years ago, Japan was our enemy.

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:32.080
The hunt's not over.

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:33.020
Hunt?

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:36.990
I'll get him this time...

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:42.130
That's a Japanese coded message

00:10:42.130 --> 00:10:44.190
we intercepted from a radio transmission.

00:10:45.340 --> 00:10:49.340
So the movements of our 
subs in the Mediterranean

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:51.300
have been leaked to Japan?

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:56.550
The codename of the spymaster 
in charge of the informants is

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:57.630
"The Magician."

00:10:58.320 --> 00:11:00.610
We should assume the leak is coming

00:11:00.610 --> 00:11:03.020
from the highest ranks of the government.

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:05.930
It's imperative we learn 
their true identities ASAP.

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:07.310
No need.

00:11:07.610 --> 00:11:08.350
Sir?

00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:12.250
The Magician has already fallen into our hands.

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:20.280
I'm impressed.

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:24.020
You've been stealing Germany's 
classified information

00:11:24.020 --> 00:11:26.240
for over six months.

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:29.310
What are you talking about?

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:31.480
I'm not a spy...

00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:33.210
This is all a mistake.

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:35.160
Our information was leaked

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:39.170
from the Japanese Imperial Army's 
General Staff Headquarters.

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:40.580
In other words,

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:43.320
your country sold you out.

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:47.180
In fact, your real name is...

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:02.310
Where... Where is he?!

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:23.520
That was the last we heard of him.

00:12:26.900 --> 00:12:30.320
It'd be impossible for a man 
that heavily injured

00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:34.240
to hide in a foreign country 
for such a long time, though.

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:37.290
Right after he escaped,

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:40.450
the sailors at Kiel revolted.

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:44.890
That triggered the revolution 
that swept across the country

00:12:44.890 --> 00:12:47.950
and ended in Germany's surrender to the Allies.

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:51.730
You're saying it was all predetermined?

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:56.280
I can't imagine any living 
man capable of such a thing.

00:12:56.940 --> 00:13:00.710
A few years ago, the Imperial Army

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:03.740
established a new intelligence agency.

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:07.180
D-Agency.

00:13:07.540 --> 00:13:10.610
Supposedly, it was founded by a 
lieutenant colonel named Yuuki,

00:13:10.610 --> 00:13:13.160
but no matter where we look, 
the truth evades us.

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:16.120
Yuuki is that man.

00:13:16.550 --> 00:13:19.770
He returned home, even after 
his country disavowed him.

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:24.780
I've never heard of such an 
organization in Japan's army...

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:26.610
Colonel.

00:13:28.230 --> 00:13:32.590
Maki was probably a spymaster, 
manipulating his accomplices.

00:13:32.590 --> 00:13:35.630
He lived in our country under 
the guise of an art dealer,

00:13:35.630 --> 00:13:37.380
contacting his informants.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:39.570
He'd gather information, analyze it,

00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:41.750
and report back home.

00:13:42.350 --> 00:13:45.790
If word gets out that Maki is dead,

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:48.430
his accomplices will start to panic,

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:51.350
and his spy network in 
Germany will break down.

00:13:51.650 --> 00:13:53.690
The only person who can prevent that

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:56.280
is him... the one giving Maki his orders.

00:13:56.880 --> 00:14:01.840
A spymaster never reveals the names 
of his sources, even to allies.

00:14:02.210 --> 00:14:06.140
Maki's got a list of his 
accomplices hidden somewhere.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:09.200
And that man...

00:14:12.050 --> 00:14:15.270
is going to come for it!

00:14:21.280 --> 00:14:22.500
As you ordered,

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:24.240
we concealed the news of Maki's death,

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:27.440
placed a notice in the newspaper 
about an unidentified body,

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:29.550
and had him placed in the Berlin Hospital.

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:34.350
Maki's home is under surveillance,

00:14:34.820 --> 00:14:37.240
and we're continuing to search it.

00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:43.780
The room in Berlin Hospital 
where he's being kept

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:46.270
is under 24/7 surveillance.

00:14:46.880 --> 00:14:49.400
We've also informed the Ministry of Aviation

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:51.250
so that we'll get a report right away

00:14:51.250 --> 00:14:54.720
if anyone calls the hospital to inquire.

00:14:57.580 --> 00:15:00.260
Did you find anything in Maki's house?

00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:01.900
No, nothing.

00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:05.310
We've investigated all his 
usual hangouts as well,

00:15:05.690 --> 00:15:08.090
but they've turned up nothing.

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:10.330
Strange...

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:12.830
We're overlooking something.

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:14.600
Colonel.

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:18.730
Colonel, you're losing your composure.

00:15:19.530 --> 00:15:20.690
What was that?

00:15:20.950 --> 00:15:23.390
There is absolutely no evidence to suggest

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:25.890
that this "Yuuki" you keep 
bringing up is the man

00:15:25.890 --> 00:15:28.260
who slipped away from you 22 years ago.

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:31.430
Furthermore, besides the matches

00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:33.330
the thief claims to have stolen,

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:36.080
there's no evidence that Maki was a spy, either.

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:38.950
I don't believe anyone who was actively spying

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:42.420
could have covered his tracks to this degree.

00:15:44.350 --> 00:15:47.940
I think you're chasing a phantom, Colonel.

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:58.350
You don't believe me, huh? But I know.

00:15:58.650 --> 00:16:01.350
I've seen the monster with my own eyes.

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:04.360
This guy has the same scent

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:06.480
as that man from 22 years ago.

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:09.930
Maki's death is just a coincidence.

00:16:09.930 --> 00:16:12.450
Faced with such an unpredictable death,

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:15.500
a spy couldn't possibly look so calm...

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:22.620
Which train was Maki on?!

00:16:23.090 --> 00:16:23.720
Huh?

00:16:24.020 --> 00:16:25.710
The one headed to Krün,

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:28.520
or the one returning to Berlin?!

00:16:29.310 --> 00:16:32.180
It was the train bound for Berlin.

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:40.530
What is it, sir?

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:44.480
<i>Maki made sure</i>

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:48.520
<i>his list wouldn't fall into enemy hands.</i>

00:16:52.680 --> 00:16:55.550
<i>In other words, on that day, he was</i>

00:16:55.550 --> 00:16:58.430
<i>on his way back after reporting 
everything he'd learned.</i>

00:17:20.250 --> 00:17:21.510
<i>Then,</i>

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:24.840
<i>the person who Maki gave 
all his information to...</i>

00:17:33.910 --> 00:17:36.140
Has anyone come to visit our man?

00:17:36.470 --> 00:17:37.870
No one.

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:48.800
Wh-What the...

00:17:48.800 --> 00:17:51.110
Nothing seems out of the ordinary.

00:17:51.110 --> 00:17:53.980
Where the hell are you looking?

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:06.690
Don't lie to me.

00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:08.480
I swear, it's true!

00:18:08.780 --> 00:18:11.360
No one except us has been in there

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:14.120
since they moved him here.

00:18:14.510 --> 00:18:16.940
Since they moved him?

00:18:18.790 --> 00:18:21.580
Yesterday, when I came here

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:23.620
to retrieve Maki's photograph,

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:27.440
I had him moved to this room so 
it'd be easier to watch him.

00:18:27.440 --> 00:18:29.190
What room was he in before?

00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:32.870
It was... 202.

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:40.800
You.

00:18:41.060 --> 00:18:43.140
Y-Yes?

00:18:43.800 --> 00:18:47.600
After the accident yesterday, 
was the only body in room 202

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:50.890
the man that's now in room 305?

00:18:52.620 --> 00:18:55.240
No, he shared that room with an elderly man

00:18:55.240 --> 00:18:57.160
who also died in the accident.

00:18:57.160 --> 00:19:00.620
Did anyone come to claim 
the body of the old man?

00:19:02.020 --> 00:19:04.920
No one. Apparently he had no relatives...

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:09.340
A little before this man here arrived,

00:19:09.340 --> 00:19:12.630
another gentleman came 
by to identify the body.

00:19:13.320 --> 00:19:14.420
What?

00:19:15.430 --> 00:19:18.220
A hat covered most of his face,

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:21.010
so I couldn't get a good look at him,

00:19:22.320 --> 00:19:26.310
but I think he might have been a foreigner.

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:46.440
Hey!

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:50.130
Where's the man named Maki being kept?

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:52.430
The Oriental who died in the train crash.

00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:54.600
Who are you...

00:19:54.900 --> 00:19:57.250
Oh, was it him?

00:19:58.360 --> 00:20:01.340
Many pardons. I had the wrong person.

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:05.480
He had a cane,

00:20:05.480 --> 00:20:07.390
and walked with a limp.

00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:15.950
Oh, and he wore a white glove on one hand.

00:20:35.140 --> 00:20:36.420
<i>When that man</i>

00:20:36.730 --> 00:20:40.070
<i>learned that Maki's train had crashed,</i>

00:20:40.070 --> 00:20:43.260
<i>he must've hopped in a car and 
rushed directly to Berlin.</i>

00:20:43.780 --> 00:20:46.920
<i>Maki had the list of his accomplices, 
the most important thing</i>

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:49.860
<i>in the world to a spymaster, 
on him at all times.</i>

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:53.340
<i>The microfilm with a copy of the list</i>

00:20:53.340 --> 00:20:56.640
<i>was sewn into the collar of his shirt.</i>

00:20:59.000 --> 00:21:01.450
<i>After that man left the hospital,</i>

00:21:01.450 --> 00:21:05.410
<i>he must've gone around contacting 
everyone on the list,</i>

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:08.500
<i>erasing any traces of evidence.</i>

00:21:11.340 --> 00:21:12.580
<i>To be a spy</i>

00:21:12.930 --> 00:21:15.610
<i>is to live alone in a foreign land,</i>

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:18.970
<i>sending information back to your homeland</i>

00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:22.090
<i>without ever letting anyone 
know who you really are.</i>

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:24.590
<i>For a spy,</i>

00:21:24.920 --> 00:21:27.380
<i>death is the end of everything.</i>

00:21:31.930 --> 00:21:35.660
<i>But even though this man 
called Maki will be buried</i>

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:38.890
<i>without anyone ever knowing 
his true identity,</i>

00:21:38.890 --> 00:21:42.340
<i>one could also say he fulfilled 
his duty as a spy.</i>

00:21:43.310 --> 00:21:45.820
<i>The information he left behind</i>

00:21:46.690 --> 00:21:48.980
<i>will live on.</i>

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:24.000
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:21.460 --> 00:23:23.680
I hear you broke up 
with your woman again.

00:23:24.130 --> 00:23:24.920
Yeah.

00:23:25.260 --> 00:23:28.600
No point in staying with one for too long.

00:23:29.800 --> 00:23:34.620
"We are all beautiful in passing," huh?

00:23:29.800 --> 00:23:34.880
Episode 12 - XX (Double Cross)
